IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa3-helpers`

-- Old Age Security Regulations (C.R.C., c. 1246), Part I (Applications): regulation 21 (what it is to reside in
-- Canada and to be present in Canada, and which absences do not interrupt either) and regulation 22 (legal residence
-- and the information prescribed for section 4.1 of the Act). The register of oas-core (item 11) names the inputs that
-- pieces oa1 and oa2 take from here: `the person resides in Canada` and `the person is present in Canada` are answered
-- by regs 21(1)(a) and 21(1)(b) below, and `the person is legally resident in Canada` by reg 22(1).
--
-- A reg 21 rule answers one limb. They are combined at the foot of the reg 21 section, in
-- `reg 21: the person resides in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations`, the way the text orders them:
-- the three "is deemed not" limbs ((2), (2.1) and (5.3)) override, and the "is considered" or "is deemed not to have
-- interrupted" limbs ((3), (4), (5.1) and (5.2)) add to the ordinary meaning of (1). The text does not say which wins
-- when they meet; that is fork F-21 in NOTES.md.
--
-- "Six months after" and "one year" are counted on the calendar with the keel's `the day that is _ after _`: a thing
-- done on the day six months after (the anniversary day) is within six months.

§ `PART I Applications`

§§ `Residence`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 21(1): the two meanings.
-- src:154 | 21 (1) For the purposes of the Act and these Regulations,
-- src:155 | (a) a person resides in Canada if he makes his home and ordinarily lives in any part of Canada; and
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(1)(a) (src:154-155)
GIVEN `the person makes his home in any part of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person ordinarily lives in any part of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(1)(a): the person resides in Canada` `the person makes his home in any part of Canada` `the person ordinarily lives in any part of Canada` MEANS
        `the person makes his home in any part of Canada`
    AND `the person ordinarily lives in any part of Canada`

-- src:156 | (b) a person is present in Canada when he is physically present in any part of Canada.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(1)(b) (src:156)
GIVEN `the person is physically present in any part of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(1)(b): the person is present in Canada` `the person is physically present in any part of Canada` MEANS
    `the person is physically present in any part of Canada`

-- 21(2): a person living on a ship outside the territorial waters of Canada is, while so living, deemed not to be living
-- in any part of Canada.
-- src:157 | (2) A person who lives on a ship outside the territorial waters of Canada shall, while so living, be deemed not to be living in any part of Canada.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(2) (src:157)
GIVEN `the person lives on a ship outside the territorial waters of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(2): the person is deemed not to be living in any part of Canada` `the person lives on a ship outside the territorial waters of Canada` MEANS
    `the person lives on a ship outside the territorial waters of Canada`

-- 21(2.1): notwithstanding (1), a person who is not a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident does not reside in Canada
-- during any period in which present in Canada for one of four purposes.
DECLARE `reg 21(2.1): Purpose for which a person is present in Canada` HAS
    `carrying out his duties as a properly accredited diplomat, consular officer, representative or official` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of a country other than Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of the United Nations or any of its agencies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of any intergovernmental organization in which Canada participates` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as a member of a military force present in Canada for training or for any other purpose in connection with the defence or security interests of Canada or under any treaty or agreement between Canada and another country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as the spouse, common-law partner or dependant of a person referred to in paragraph (a) or (b), or the dependant of that person's spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as a member of the staff of or as a person otherwise accompanying a person referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:158 | (2.1) Notwithstanding subsection (1), a person who is not a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident of Canada does not reside in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations during any period in which he is present in Canada
-- src:159 | (a) for the purpose of carrying out his duties as a properly accredited diplomat, consular officer, representative or official of
-- src:160 | (i) a country other than Canada,
-- src:161 | (ii) the United Nations or any of its agencies, or
-- src:162 | (iii) any intergovernmental organization in which Canada participates;
-- src:163 | (b) as a member of a military force present in Canada for training or for any other purpose in connection with the defence or security interests of Canada or under any treaty or agreement between Canada and another country;
-- src:164 | (c) as the spouse, common-law partner or dependant of a person referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) or the dependant of that person’s spouse or common-law partner; or
-- src:165 | (d) as a member of the staff of or as a person otherwise accompanying a person referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c).
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(2.1) (src:158-165)
GIVEN `the person is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is present in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `reg 21(2.1): Purpose for which a person is present in Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(2.1): the person does not reside in Canada during the period` `the person is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident of Canada` `the person is present in Canada` purpose MEANS
        (NOT `the person is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident of Canada`)
    AND `the person is present in Canada`
    AND (   (    purpose's `carrying out his duties as a properly accredited diplomat, consular officer, representative or official`
             AND (   purpose's `of a country other than Canada`
                  OR purpose's `of the United Nations or any of its agencies`
                  OR purpose's `of any intergovernmental organization in which Canada participates`))
         OR purpose's `as a member of a military force present in Canada for training or for any other purpose in connection with the defence or security interests of Canada or under any treaty or agreement between Canada and another country`
         OR purpose's `as the spouse, common-law partner or dependant of a person referred to in paragraph (a) or (b), or the dependant of that person's spouse or common-law partner`
         OR purpose's `as a member of the staff of or as a person otherwise accompanying a person referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 21(3): a spouse or common-law partner who joins, outside Canada, a person residing in Canada who is absent in a
-- circumstance of (5)(a) or (b). The first limb ("returned in time") is the same wording as (5)(c)(i) and (5)(f)(i), which
-- call this rule: the thing that came back is the one who joined; the other is the person it is measured against.
-- src:167 | (a) the spouse or common-law partner returns to Canada either before or within six months after the return of the person residing in Canada or within six months after that person’s death if that person dies while so absent from Canada; or
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(3)(a) (src:167)
GIVEN `the day on which the person returns to Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the other person returned to Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the other person died while so absent from Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(3)(a): the person returns to Canada before or within six months after the return of the other person, or within six months after that person's death` `the day on which the person returns to Canada` `the day on which the other person returned to Canada` `the day on which the other person died while so absent from Canada` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the person returns to Canada`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST back THEN
            `no later than six months after` back `the day on which the other person returned to Canada`
        OR  `no later than six months after` back `the day on which the other person died while so absent from Canada`
    WHERE
        `no later than six months after` day anchor MEANS
            CONSIDER anchor
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST a THEN day AT MOST (`the day that is` (`a limit in months` 6) `after` a)

-- src:166 | (3) For the purposes of the Act and these Regulations, where a person becomes the spouse or common-law partner of a person residing in Canada while the person residing in Canada is absent from Canada in any of the circumstances specified in paragraph (5)(a) or (b), the period outside Canada of the spouse after their marriage or of the common-law partner after becoming such a partner is considered a period of residence and presence in Canada, if
-- src:167 | (a) the spouse or common-law partner returns to Canada either before or within six months after the return of the person residing in Canada or within six months after that person’s death if that person dies while so absent from Canada; or
-- src:168 | (b) the spouse or common-law partner attains, during that period outside Canada, an age at which the spouse or common-law partner is eligible to be paid a pension under the Act.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(3) (src:166-168)
GIVEN `the person became the spouse or common-law partner of a person residing in Canada while that person was absent from Canada in a circumstance specified in paragraph (5)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person returns to Canada in time under paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 21(3)(a) above
      `the person attains, during that period outside Canada, an age at which the person is eligible to be paid a pension under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(3): the period outside Canada is considered a period of residence and presence in Canada` `the person became the spouse or common-law partner of a person residing in Canada while that person was absent from Canada in a circumstance specified in paragraph (5)(a) or (b)` `the person returns to Canada in time under paragraph (a)` `the person attains, during that period outside Canada, an age at which the person is eligible to be paid a pension under the Act` MEANS
        `the person became the spouse or common-law partner of a person residing in Canada while that person was absent from Canada in a circumstance specified in paragraph (5)(a) or (b)`
    AND (   `the person returns to Canada in time under paragraph (a)`
         OR `the person attains, during that period outside Canada, an age at which the person is eligible to be paid a pension under the Act`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 21(5): the circumstances. The six paragraphs are each their own rule on their own facts.
-- (a): employed out of Canada by one of six employers, if during the employment he had a place of abode in Canada
-- to which he intended to return or kept a self-contained domestic establishment there, and he returned within six
-- months after the employment ended or attained pension age while so employed.
DECLARE `reg 21(5)(a): Employer of a person employed out of Canada` IS ONE OF
    `reg 21(5)(a)(i): the United Nations or one of its specialized agencies`
    `reg 21(5)(a)(ii): the North Atlantic Treaty Organization`
    `reg 21(5)(a)(iii): the Commonwealth Secretariat`
    `reg 21(5)(a)(iv): the Organization of Economic Cooperation and Development`
    `reg 21(5)(a)(v): l'Agence de coopération culturelle et technique`
    `reg 21(5)(a)(vi): a Canadian firm or corporation, as a representative or member thereof`
    `reg 21(5)(a): Another employer`

DECLARE `reg 21(5)(a): Facts about employment out of Canada` HAS
    employer IS A `reg 21(5)(a): Employer of a person employed out of Canada`
    `had in Canada a permanent place of abode to which he intended to return` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maintained in Canada a self-contained domestic establishment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day on which his employment out of Canada ended` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day on which he returned to Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `attained, while employed out of Canada, an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:175 | (a) while that person was employed out of Canada
-- src:176 | (i) by the United Nations or one of its specialized agencies,
-- src:177 | (ii) by the North Atlantic Treaty Organization,
-- src:178 | (iii) by the Commonwealth Secretariat,
-- src:179 | (iv) by the Organization of Economic Cooperation and Development,
-- src:180 | (v) by l’Agence de coopération culturelle et technique, or
-- src:181 | (vi) by a Canadian firm or corporation as a representative or member thereof,
-- src:182 | if during his employment out of Canada he
-- src:183 | (vii) had in Canada a permanent place of abode to which he intended to return, or
-- src:184 | (viii) maintained in Canada a self-contained domestic establishment,
-- src:185 | and he returned to Canada within six months after the end of his employment out of Canada or he attained, while employed out of Canada, an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act;
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(5)(a) (src:175-185)
GIVEN employment IS A `reg 21(5)(a): Facts about employment out of Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(5)(a): the absence is in the circumstance of employment out of Canada` employment MEANS
        `the employer is one of the six` (employment's employer)
    AND (   employment's `had in Canada a permanent place of abode to which he intended to return`
         OR employment's `maintained in Canada a self-contained domestic establishment`)
    AND (   `returned within six months` employment
         OR employment's `attained, while employed out of Canada, an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act`)
    WHERE
        `the employer is one of the six` e MEANS
            CONSIDER e
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(a)(i): the United Nations or one of its specialized agencies` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(a)(ii): the North Atlantic Treaty Organization` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(a)(iii): the Commonwealth Secretariat` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(a)(iv): the Organization of Economic Cooperation and Development` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(a)(v): l'Agence de coopération culturelle et technique` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(a)(vi): a Canadian firm or corporation, as a representative or member thereof` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(a): Another employer` THEN FALSE
        `returned within six months` x MEANS
            CONSIDER x's `the day on which his employment out of Canada ended`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST ended THEN
                CONSIDER x's `the day on which he returned to Canada`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                WHEN JUST back THEN back AT MOST (`the day that is` (`a limit in months` 6) `after` ended)

-- (b): employed or engaged out of Canada in one of nine ways; the same two conditions as (a) for the return, but no
-- condition about a place of abode.
DECLARE `reg 21(5)(b): Employment or engagement of a person out of Canada` IS ONE OF
    `reg 21(5)(b)(i): the Government of Canada or the government or a municipal corporation of any province`
    `reg 21(5)(b)(ii): the performance of services in another country under a development or assistance program sponsored or operated there by the Government of Canada or of a province or by a non-profit Canadian agency`
    `reg 21(5)(b)(iii): as a member of the Canadian Forces, pursuant to and in connection with the requirements of his duties`
    `reg 21(5)(b)(iv): work for Canada connected with the prosecution of any war`
    `reg 21(5)(b)(v): as a member of the armed forces of any ally of Canada during any war`
    `reg 21(5)(b)(vi): as a missionary with any religious group or organization`
    `reg 21(5)(b)(vii): as a worker in lumbering, harvesting, fishing or other seasonal employment`
    `reg 21(5)(b)(viii): as a transport worker on trains, aircraft, ships or buses running between Canada and points outside Canada or other similar employment`
    `reg 21(5)(b)(ix): as an employee, a member or an officer of an international charitable organization`
    `reg 21(5)(b): Another employment or engagement`

DECLARE `reg 21(5)(b): Facts about employment or engagement out of Canada` HAS
    kind IS A `reg 21(5)(b): Employment or engagement of a person out of Canada`
    `the day on which his employment or engagement out of Canada ended` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day on which he returned to Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `attained, while employed or engaged out of Canada, an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:186 | (b) while that person was employed or engaged out of Canada
-- src:187 | (i) by the Government of Canada or of the government or a municipal corporation of any province,
-- src:188 | (ii) in the performance of services in another country under a development or assistance program that is sponsored or operated in that country by the Government of Canada or of a province or by a non-profit Canadian agency,
-- src:189 | (iii) as a member of the Canadian Forces, pursuant to and in connection with the requirements of his duties,
-- src:190 | (iv) in work for Canada connected with the prosecution of any war,
-- src:191 | (v) as a member of the armed forces of any ally of Canada during any war,
-- src:192 | (vi) as a missionary with any religious group or organization,
-- src:193 | (vii) as a worker in lumbering, harvesting, fishing or other seasonal employment,
-- src:194 | (viii) as a transport worker on trains, aircraft, ships or buses running between Canada and points outside Canada or other similar employment, or
-- src:195 | (ix) as an employee, a member or an officer of an international charitable organization,
-- src:196 | if he returned to Canada within six months of the end of his employment or engagement out of Canada or he attained, while employed or engaged out of Canada, an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act;
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(5)(b) (src:186-196)
GIVEN engagement IS A `reg 21(5)(b): Facts about employment or engagement out of Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(5)(b): the absence is in the circumstance of employment or engagement out of Canada` engagement MEANS
        `the kind is one of the nine` (engagement's kind)
    AND (   `returned within six months` engagement
         OR engagement's `attained, while employed or engaged out of Canada, an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act`)
    WHERE
        `the kind is one of the nine` k MEANS
            CONSIDER k
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(b)(i): the Government of Canada or the government or a municipal corporation of any province` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(b)(ii): the performance of services in another country under a development or assistance program sponsored or operated there by the Government of Canada or of a province or by a non-profit Canadian agency` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(b)(iii): as a member of the Canadian Forces, pursuant to and in connection with the requirements of his duties` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(b)(iv): work for Canada connected with the prosecution of any war` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(b)(v): as a member of the armed forces of any ally of Canada during any war` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(b)(vi): as a missionary with any religious group or organization` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(b)(vii): as a worker in lumbering, harvesting, fishing or other seasonal employment` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(b)(viii): as a transport worker on trains, aircraft, ships or buses running between Canada and points outside Canada or other similar employment` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(b)(ix): as an employee, a member or an officer of an international charitable organization` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 21(5)(b): Another employment or engagement` THEN FALSE
        `returned within six months` x MEANS
            CONSIDER x's `the day on which his employment or engagement out of Canada ended`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST ended THEN
                CONSIDER x's `the day on which he returned to Canada`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                WHEN JUST back THEN back AT MOST (`the day that is` (`a limit in months` 6) `after` ended)

-- (c): accompanying a spouse or common-law partner who was absent in a circumstance of (a) or (b), or in order to
-- attend school or university; (i) returned in time (the (3)(a) test), or (ii) attained pension age while absent.
DECLARE `reg 21(5)(c): Facts about accompanying a spouse or common-law partner` HAS
    `accompanying their spouse or common-law partner who was absent from Canada in a circumstance specified in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accompanying their spouse or common-law partner who was absent from Canada for the purpose of attending school or university` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day on which the person returned to Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day on which their spouse or common-law partner returned to Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day on which their spouse or common-law partner died while so absent from Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `while so absent from Canada, attained an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:197 | (c) while that person was accompanying their spouse or common-law partner who was absent from Canada in any of the circumstances specified in paragraph (a) or (b) or for the purpose of attending school or university, if that person
-- src:198 | (i) returned to Canada either before or within six months after the return of their spouse or common-law partner or within six months after the death of their spouse or common-law partner, if their spouse or common-law partner died while so absent from Canada, or
-- src:199 | (ii) while so absent from Canada, attained an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act;
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(5)(c) (src:197-199)
GIVEN accompanying IS A `reg 21(5)(c): Facts about accompanying a spouse or common-law partner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(5)(c): the absence is in the circumstance of accompanying a spouse or common-law partner` accompanying MEANS
        (   accompanying's `accompanying their spouse or common-law partner who was absent from Canada in a circumstance specified in paragraph (a) or (b)`
         OR accompanying's `accompanying their spouse or common-law partner who was absent from Canada for the purpose of attending school or university`)
    AND (   `reg 21(3)(a): the person returns to Canada before or within six months after the return of the other person, or within six months after that person's death` (accompanying's `the day on which the person returned to Canada`) (accompanying's `the day on which their spouse or common-law partner returned to Canada`) (accompanying's `the day on which their spouse or common-law partner died while so absent from Canada`)
         OR accompanying's `while so absent from Canada, attained an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act`)

-- (d): awaiting transportation to Canada during or immediately after World War II.
DECLARE `reg 21(5)(d): Facts about awaiting transportation to Canada` HAS
    `awaiting transportation to Canada during or immediately after World War II` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unable to return to Canada owing to the dislocation of transportation facilities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `returned to Canada when transportation became available` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:200 | (d) while that person was awaiting transportation to Canada during or immediately after World War II, if he
-- src:201 | (i) was unable to return to Canada owing to the dislocation of transportation facilities, and
-- src:202 | (ii) returned to Canada when transportation became available;
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(5)(d) (src:200-202)
GIVEN awaiting IS A `reg 21(5)(d): Facts about awaiting transportation to Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(5)(d): the absence is in the circumstance of awaiting transportation to Canada` awaiting MEANS
        awaiting's `awaiting transportation to Canada during or immediately after World War II`
    AND awaiting's `unable to return to Canada owing to the dislocation of transportation facilities`
    AND awaiting's `returned to Canada when transportation became available`

-- (e): the same, accompanying a spouse (the paragraph says "spouse" only) who was resident in Canada.
DECLARE `reg 21(5)(e): Facts about accompanying a spouse awaiting transportation to Canada` HAS
    `accompanying his spouse who was resident in Canada and awaiting transportation to Canada during or immediately after World War II` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unable to return to Canada owing to the dislocation of transportation facilities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `returned to Canada when transportation became available` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:203 | (e) while that person was accompanying his spouse who was resident in Canada and awaiting transportation to Canada during or immediately after World War II, if that person
-- src:204 | (i) was unable to return to Canada owing to the dislocation of transportation facilities, and
-- src:205 | (ii) returned to Canada when transportation became available; or
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(5)(e) (src:203-205)
GIVEN accompanying IS A `reg 21(5)(e): Facts about accompanying a spouse awaiting transportation to Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(5)(e): the absence is in the circumstance of accompanying a spouse awaiting transportation to Canada` accompanying MEANS
        accompanying's `accompanying his spouse who was resident in Canada and awaiting transportation to Canada during or immediately after World War II`
    AND accompanying's `unable to return to Canada owing to the dislocation of transportation facilities`
    AND accompanying's `returned to Canada when transportation became available`

-- (f): a dependent person accompanying, and residing outside Canada with, the person on whom they were dependent, who
-- resided in Canada and was absent in a circumstance of (a) or (b).
DECLARE `reg 21(5)(f): Facts about a dependent person accompanying the person on whom they depend` HAS
    `a dependent person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accompanying and residing outside Canada with the person on whom he was dependent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person on whom he was dependent resided in Canada and was absent from Canada in a circumstance specified in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day on which the dependent person returned to Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day on which the person on whom he was dependent returned to Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day on which the person on whom he was dependent died while so absent from Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `while so absent from Canada, attained an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:206 | (f) while that person was a dependent person and was accompanying and residing outside Canada with the person on whom he was dependent, if the person on whom he was dependent resided in Canada and was absent from Canada in any of the circumstances specified in paragraph (a) or (b) and if the dependent person
-- src:207 | (i) returned to Canada before or within six months after the return of the person on whom he was dependent or within six months after that person’s death, if that person died while so absent from Canada, or
-- src:208 | (ii) while so absent from Canada, attained an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(5)(f) (src:206-208)
GIVEN dependent IS A `reg 21(5)(f): Facts about a dependent person accompanying the person on whom they depend`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(5)(f): the absence is in the circumstance of a dependent person accompanying the person on whom they depend` dependent MEANS
        dependent's `a dependent person`
    AND dependent's `accompanying and residing outside Canada with the person on whom he was dependent`
    AND dependent's `the person on whom he was dependent resided in Canada and was absent from Canada in a circumstance specified in paragraph (a) or (b)`
    AND (   `reg 21(3)(a): the person returns to Canada before or within six months after the return of the other person, or within six months after that person's death` (dependent's `the day on which the dependent person returned to Canada`) (dependent's `the day on which the person on whom he was dependent returned to Canada`) (dependent's `the day on which the person on whom he was dependent died while so absent from Canada`)
         OR dependent's `while so absent from Canada, attained an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act`)

-- 21(5) as a whole: the absence is one of the six circumstances.
-- src:174 | (5) The absences from Canada referred to in paragraph (4)(c) of a person residing in Canada are absences under the following circumstances:
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(5) (src:174)
GIVEN `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(5): the absence is one of the absences specified in subsection (5)` `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (a)` `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (b)` `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (c)` `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (d)` `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (e)` `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (f)` MEANS
        `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (a)`
    OR  `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (b)`
    OR  `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (c)`
    OR  `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (d)`
    OR  `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (e)`
    OR  `the absence is in a circumstance of paragraph (f)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 21(4): an interval of absence of a person resident in Canada that (a) is temporary and does not exceed one year, (b) is
-- to attend a school or university, or (c) is specified in (5) is deemed not to have interrupted residence or presence.
-- "Does not exceed one year": the interval's last day is on or before the day one year after its first (fork F-21(4)).
-- src:169 | (4) Any interval of absence from Canada of a person resident in Canada that is
-- src:170 | (a) of a temporary nature and does not exceed one year,
-- src:171 | (b) for the purpose of attending a school or university, or
-- src:172 | (c) specified in subsection (5)
-- src:173 | shall be deemed not to have interrupted that person’s residence or presence in Canada.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(4) (src:169-173)
GIVEN `the person was resident in Canada before the interval of absence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interval of absence is of a temporary nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the interval of absence from Canada` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the interval of absence from Canada` IS A DATE
      `the interval of absence is for the purpose of attending a school or university` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interval of absence is specified in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(4): the interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence or presence in Canada` `the person was resident in Canada before the interval of absence` `the interval of absence is of a temporary nature` `the first day of the interval of absence from Canada` `the last day of the interval of absence from Canada` `the interval of absence is for the purpose of attending a school or university` `the interval of absence is specified in subsection (5)` MEANS
        `the person was resident in Canada before the interval of absence`
    AND (   (    `the interval of absence is of a temporary nature`
             AND `the last day of the interval of absence from Canada` AT MOST (`the day that is` (`a limit in years` 1) `after` `the first day of the interval of absence from Canada`))
         OR `the interval of absence is for the purpose of attending a school or university`
         OR `the interval of absence is specified in subsection (5)`)

