-- 21(5.1) to (5.3): persons covered by an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act (the agreements are in the
-- Schedule: see oa3-part1-agreements.l4).
-- (5.1): for the purposes of an allowance, the absence of a person who is subject to the Act while residing in another
-- country by virtue of an agreement, and of the spouse, common-law partner or dependants living with them there, is not
-- considered to have interrupted residence or presence in Canada.
-- src:209 | (5.1) Where, by virtue of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act, a person is subject to the Act while residing in a country other than Canada, the absence from Canada of that person, the person’s spouse or common-law partner and the dependants of the person or of the person’s spouse or common-law partner, if the spouse, common-law partner or dependants, as the case may be, reside with the person in that country, shall, for the purposes of an allowance, not be considered to have interrupted the residence or presence in Canada of the person, spouse, common-law partner or dependants.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(5.1) (src:209)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the Act while residing in a country other than Canada by virtue of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the absent person is that person, or their spouse or common-law partner or a dependant of either, residing with that person in that country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is asked for the purposes of an allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(5.1): the absence is not considered to have interrupted the residence or presence in Canada` `the person is subject to the Act while residing in a country other than Canada by virtue of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act` `the absent person is that person, or their spouse or common-law partner or a dependant of either, residing with that person in that country` `the question is asked for the purposes of an allowance` MEANS
        `the person is subject to the Act while residing in a country other than Canada by virtue of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act`
    AND `the absent person is that person, or their spouse or common-law partner or a dependant of either, residing with that person in that country`
    AND `the question is asked for the purposes of an allowance`

-- (5.2): where a person resident in Canada is subject to the legislation of another country by virtue of an agreement, a
-- period of pensionable employment of the spouse, common-law partner or a dependant under the Canada Pension Plan or a
-- provincial comprehensive plan is considered a period of residence in Canada (whose residence: fork F-21(5.2)).
-- src:210 | (5.2) Where a person who is resident in Canada is subject to the legislation of a country other than Canada by virtue of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act, and the person’s spouse or common-law partner or the dependant of the person or of the person’s spouse or common-law partner engages in pensionable employment as defined in the Canada Pension Plan or in the plan of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan, any period in such pensionable employment shall, for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations, be considered to be a period of residence in Canada.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(5.2) (src:210)
GIVEN `the person who is resident in Canada is subject to the legislation of a country other than Canada by virtue of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's spouse or common-law partner, or a dependant of the person or of the spouse or common-law partner, engages in pensionable employment as defined in the Canada Pension Plan or in the plan of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(5.2): the period of pensionable employment is considered a period of residence in Canada` `the person who is resident in Canada is subject to the legislation of a country other than Canada by virtue of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act` `the person's spouse or common-law partner, or a dependant of the person or of the spouse or common-law partner, engages in pensionable employment as defined in the Canada Pension Plan or in the plan of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` MEANS
        `the person who is resident in Canada is subject to the legislation of a country other than Canada by virtue of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act`
    AND `the person's spouse or common-law partner, or a dependant of the person or of the spouse or common-law partner, engages in pensionable employment as defined in the Canada Pension Plan or in the plan of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`

-- (5.3): a person subject to the legislation of another country by virtue of an agreement is deemed not to be resident
-- in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations.
-- src:211 | (5.3) Where, by virtue of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act, a person is subject to the legislation of a country other than Canada, that person shall, for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations, be deemed not to be resident in Canada.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(5.3) (src:211)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the legislation of a country other than Canada by virtue of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(5.3): the person is deemed not to be resident in Canada` `the person is subject to the legislation of a country other than Canada by virtue of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act` MEANS
    `the person is subject to the legislation of a country other than Canada by virtue of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act`

