-- 21(6) and (7): the relatives who are "dependent persons" and "dependants". The two lists are the same ten relatives
-- (6: "that person's father, mother, brother, sister, child or foster child or the father, mother, child or foster child
-- of the person's spouse or common-law partner"; 7 repeats the words), so the relatives are declared once, under 21(6).
-- src:212 | (6) For the purposes of paragraph (5)(f), dependent person means, with respect to a person who was absent from Canada in any of the circumstances specified in paragraph (5)(a) or (b), that person’s father, mother, brother, sister, child or foster child or the father, mother, child or foster child of the person’s spouse or common-law partner.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(6) (src:212)
DECLARE `reg 21(6): Relative of a person` IS ONE OF
    `reg 21(6): the person's father`
    `reg 21(6): the person's mother`
    `reg 21(6): the person's brother`
    `reg 21(6): the person's sister`
    `reg 21(6): the person's child`
    `reg 21(6): the person's foster child`
    `reg 21(6): the father of the person's spouse or common-law partner`
    `reg 21(6): the mother of the person's spouse or common-law partner`
    `reg 21(6): the child of the person's spouse or common-law partner`
    `reg 21(6): the foster child of the person's spouse or common-law partner`
    `reg 21(6): Another relative or no relative`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(6) (src:212)
GIVEN relative IS A `reg 21(6): Relative of a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(6): the relative is one of the ten` relative MEANS
    CONSIDER relative
    WHEN `reg 21(6): the person's father` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reg 21(6): the person's mother` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reg 21(6): the person's brother` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reg 21(6): the person's sister` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reg 21(6): the person's child` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reg 21(6): the person's foster child` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reg 21(6): the father of the person's spouse or common-law partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reg 21(6): the mother of the person's spouse or common-law partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reg 21(6): the child of the person's spouse or common-law partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reg 21(6): the foster child of the person's spouse or common-law partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reg 21(6): Another relative or no relative` THEN FALSE

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(6) (src:212)
GIVEN `the person was absent from Canada in a circumstance specified in paragraph (5)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      relative IS A `reg 21(6): Relative of a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(6): the relative is a dependent person for the purposes of paragraph (5)(f)` `the person was absent from Canada in a circumstance specified in paragraph (5)(a) or (b)` relative MEANS
        `the person was absent from Canada in a circumstance specified in paragraph (5)(a) or (b)`
    AND `reg 21(6): the relative is one of the ten` relative

-- src:213 | (7) Dependant means
-- src:214 | (a) with respect to a person who does not reside in Canada within the meaning of subsection (2.1),
-- src:215 | (b) with respect to a person who is deemed to be resident in Canada within the meaning of subsection (5.1), or
-- src:216 | (c) with respect to a person referred to in subsection (5.2) who, while resident in Canada is subject to the legislation of a country other than Canada,
-- src:217 | that person’s father, mother, brother, sister, child or foster child or the father, mother, child or foster child of the person’s spouse or common-law partner.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(7) (src:213-217)
GIVEN `the person does not reside in Canada within the meaning of subsection (2.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is deemed to be resident in Canada within the meaning of subsection (5.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person referred to in subsection (5.2) who, while resident in Canada, is subject to the legislation of a country other than Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      relative IS A `reg 21(6): Relative of a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(7): the relative is a dependant` `the person does not reside in Canada within the meaning of subsection (2.1)` `the person is deemed to be resident in Canada within the meaning of subsection (5.1)` `the person is a person referred to in subsection (5.2) who, while resident in Canada, is subject to the legislation of a country other than Canada` relative MEANS
        (   `the person does not reside in Canada within the meaning of subsection (2.1)`
         OR `the person is deemed to be resident in Canada within the meaning of subsection (5.1)`
         OR `the person is a person referred to in subsection (5.2) who, while resident in Canada, is subject to the legislation of a country other than Canada`)
    AND `reg 21(6): the relative is one of the ten` relative

