-- 21(8) and (9): the information prescribed for section 4.1 of the Act as it relates to subparagraph 3(1)(c)(iii) of the Act:
-- forty years of contribution or its equivalent in the Canada Pension Plan or the Quebec Pension Plan. The terms (9) borrows
-- from those plans (basic exemption, contributory period, unadjusted pensionable earnings, family allowance recipient,
-- personal exemption, recipient of family benefits) are asked as facts about each calendar year, as the guide asks
-- for borrowed terms: this record is where reg 21(9) is encoded.
-- src:226 | (9) For the purposes of subsection (8),
-- src:227 | (a) in relation to the Canada Pension Plan, basic exemption, contributory period and unadjusted pensionable earnings have the same meaning as in subsection 2(1) of that Act and family allowance recipient has the same meaning as in subsection 42(1) of that Act; and
-- src:228 | (b) in relation to An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan, R.S.Q., c. R-9, recipient of family benefits, personal exemption, unadjusted pensionable earnings and contributory period have the same meaning as in paragraph 1(v) and sections 43, 98 and 101 of that Act respectively.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(9) (src:226-228)
DECLARE `reg 21(8): Facts about a calendar year` HAS
    `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
    `had unadjusted pensionable earnings above the basic exemption (Canada Pension Plan) or the personal exemption (Quebec Pension Plan) for that year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `received a retirement pension or disability pension under the Canada Pension Plan or An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had time excluded from a contributory period because a family allowance recipient, or time not included in a contributory period because a recipient of family benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
    `filed an income tax return as a resident of Canada with the Minister of National Revenue` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:219 | (a) in the case of a person who is in receipt of or has been approved for a retirement, disability or survivor’s pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a retirement, disability or surviving spouse’s pension under An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan, CQLR, c. R-9, information indicating that the person, for at least 40 years, for all or part of each of those years,
-- src:220 | (i) had unadjusted pensionable earnings under the Canada Pension Plan that were above the person’s basic exemption for that year, or had unadjusted pensionable earnings under An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan that were above the person’s personal exemption for that year,
-- src:221 | (ii) received a retirement pension or disability pension under either the Canada Pension Plan or An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan, or
-- src:222 | (iii) had time excluded from a contributory period under the Canada Pension Plan because the person was a family allowance recipient, or had time not included in a contributory period under An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan because the person was a recipient of family benefits; or
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(8)(a)(i) to (iii) (src:219-222)
GIVEN year IS A `reg 21(8): Facts about a calendar year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(8)(a): the year counts toward the forty years` year MEANS
        year's `had unadjusted pensionable earnings above the basic exemption (Canada Pension Plan) or the personal exemption (Quebec Pension Plan) for that year`
    OR  year's `received a retirement pension or disability pension under the Canada Pension Plan or An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan`
    OR  year's `had time excluded from a contributory period because a family allowance recipient, or time not included in a contributory period because a recipient of family benefits`

-- (a): a person in receipt of or approved for a retirement, disability or survivor's pension under the Canada Pension Plan or the
-- Quebec Pension Plan: information indicating that, for at least 40 years, for all or part of each, one of (i), (ii) or (iii) held.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(8)(a) (src:219-222)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `reg 21(8): Facts about a calendar year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(8)(a): the information indicates forty years` years MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN y YIELD `reg 21(8)(a): the year counts toward the forty years` y) years) AT LEAST 40

-- (b): a person not in receipt of and not approved for such a pension: the same forty years, and a tax return as a
-- resident of Canada for the most recent calendar year for which the filing due date has passed and for at least 40 of
-- those years other than 1969, 1970 and 1971.
-- src:223 | (b) in the case of a person who is not in receipt of and has not been approved for a retirement, disability or survivor’s pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a retirement, disability or surviving spouse’s pension under An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan, CQLR, c. R-9, information indicating that the person,
-- src:224 | (i) for at least 40 years, for all or part of each of those years, met the requirements set out in subparagraph (a)(i), (ii) or (iii), and
-- src:225 | (ii) for the most recent calendar year for which the filing due date has passed and for at least 40 of the years referred to in subparagraph (i), other than for 1969, 1970 and 1971, filed an income tax return as a resident of Canada with the Minister of National Revenue.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(8)(b) (src:223-225)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `reg 21(8): Facts about a calendar year`
      `the person filed an income tax return as a resident of Canada for the most recent calendar year for which the filing due date has passed` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the Income Tax Act, which sets the filing due date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(8)(b): the information indicates forty years and returns filed` years `the person filed an income tax return as a resident of Canada for the most recent calendar year for which the filing due date has passed` MEANS
        `reg 21(8)(a): the information indicates forty years` years
    AND `the person filed an income tax return as a resident of Canada for the most recent calendar year for which the filing due date has passed`
    AND count (filter `a year whose return counts` years) AT LEAST 40
    WHERE
        `a year whose return counts` y MEANS
                `reg 21(8)(a): the year counts toward the forty years` y
            AND y's `filed an income tax return as a resident of Canada with the Minister of National Revenue`
            AND ((NOT (y's `calendar year` EQUALS 1969)) AND (NOT (y's `calendar year` EQUALS 1970)) AND (NOT (y's `calendar year` EQUALS 1971)))

-- src:218 | (8) For the purposes of section 4.1 of the Act as it relates to the requirement of subparagraph 3(1)(c)(iii) of the Act, the prescribed information is,
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(8) (src:218)
GIVEN `the person is in receipt of or has been approved for a retirement, disability or survivor's pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a retirement, disability or surviving spouse's pension under An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      years IS A LIST OF `reg 21(8): Facts about a calendar year`
      `the person filed an income tax return as a resident of Canada for the most recent calendar year for which the filing due date has passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21(8): the prescribed information for subparagraph 3(1)(c)(iii) of the Act has been made available` `the person is in receipt of or has been approved for a retirement, disability or survivor's pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a retirement, disability or surviving spouse's pension under An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan` years `the person filed an income tax return as a resident of Canada for the most recent calendar year for which the filing due date has passed` MEANS
    IF `the person is in receipt of or has been approved for a retirement, disability or survivor's pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a retirement, disability or surviving spouse's pension under An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan`
    THEN `reg 21(8)(a): the information indicates forty years` years
    ELSE `reg 21(8)(b): the information indicates forty years and returns filed` years `the person filed an income tax return as a resident of Canada for the most recent calendar year for which the filing due date has passed`

