-- 21 as a whole. The deeming limbs are combined as the text orders them (fork F-21 in NOTES.md): "notwithstanding subsection
-- (1)" in (2.1), "deemed not to be living" in (2) and "deemed not to be resident" in (5.3) override; "considered a period
-- of residence" in (3) and (5.2) and "deemed not to have interrupted" in (4) and (5.1) add to the meaning in (1)(a).
-- src:154 | 21 (1) For the purposes of the Act and these Regulations,
-- src:155 | (a) a person resides in Canada if he makes his home and ordinarily lives in any part of Canada; and
-- src:156 | (b) a person is present in Canada when he is physically present in any part of Canada.
-- src:157 | (2) A person who lives on a ship outside the territorial waters of Canada shall, while so living, be deemed not to be living in any part of Canada.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(1) and (2) (src:154-157)
GIVEN `the person resides in Canada under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is deemed not to be living in any part of Canada under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not reside in Canada under subsection (2.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is deemed not to be resident in Canada under subsection (5.3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence under subsection (4) or (5.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a period is considered a period of residence in Canada under subsection (3) or (5.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21: the person resides in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` `the person resides in Canada under paragraph (1)(a)` `the person is deemed not to be living in any part of Canada under subsection (2)` `the person does not reside in Canada under subsection (2.1)` `the person is deemed not to be resident in Canada under subsection (5.3)` `an interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence under subsection (4) or (5.1)` `a period is considered a period of residence in Canada under subsection (3) or (5.2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the person is deemed not to be living in any part of Canada under subsection (2)`)
    AND (NOT `the person does not reside in Canada under subsection (2.1)`)
    AND (NOT `the person is deemed not to be resident in Canada under subsection (5.3)`)
    AND (   `the person resides in Canada under paragraph (1)(a)`
         OR `an interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence under subsection (4) or (5.1)`
         OR `a period is considered a period of residence in Canada under subsection (3) or (5.2)`)

-- src:154 | 21 (1) For the purposes of the Act and these Regulations,
-- src:155 | (a) a person resides in Canada if he makes his home and ordinarily lives in any part of Canada; and
-- src:156 | (b) a person is present in Canada when he is physically present in any part of Canada.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 21(1)(b) (src:154) (src:156)
GIVEN `the person is present in Canada under paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's presence under subsection (4) or (5.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a period is considered a period of presence in Canada under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
