§§ `Legal Residence`

-- 22(1): "legal residence" for subsections 4(1), 19(2) and 21(2) of the Act: on the applicable day the person (a) is or was
-- lawfully in Canada under the immigration laws in force that day; or (b) is or was resident and absent, the absence being
-- deemed not to have interrupted residence, and was lawfully in Canada immediately before the absence began; or (c) is
-- not resident but is deemed resident. The "applicable day" is the day those subsections of the Act name (out of range:
-- sections 4(1), 19(2) and 21(2), pieces oa1 and oa2), so every fact below is a fact on that day.
-- src:231 | 22 (1) For the purposes of subsections 4(1), 19(2) and 21(2) of the Act, legal residence, with respect to a person described in any of those subsections, means that, on the applicable day specified in paragraph (a) or (b) of those subsections, that person
-- src:232 | (a) is or was lawfully in Canada pursuant to the immigration laws of Canada in force on that day;
-- src:233 | (b) is or was a resident of Canada and is or was absent from Canada, but
-- src:234 | (i) is deemed, pursuant to subsection 21(4) or (5) or under the terms of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act, not to have interrupted the person’s residence in Canada during that absence, and
-- src:235 | (ii) was lawfully in Canada pursuant to the immigration laws of Canada immediately prior to the commencement of the absence; or
-- src:236 | (c) is not or was not resident of Canada but is deemed, pursuant to subsection 21(3) or under the terms of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act, to be or to have been resident in Canada.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 22(1) (src:231-236)
GIVEN `the person is or was lawfully in Canada pursuant to the immigration laws of Canada in force on the applicable day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is or was a resident of Canada and is or was absent from Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is deemed, pursuant to subsection 21(4) or (5) or under the terms of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act, not to have interrupted the person's residence in Canada during that absence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was lawfully in Canada pursuant to the immigration laws of Canada immediately prior to the commencement of the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not or was not resident of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is deemed, pursuant to subsection 21(3) or under the terms of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act, to be or to have been resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 22(1): the person is legally resident in Canada` `the person is or was lawfully in Canada pursuant to the immigration laws of Canada in force on the applicable day` `the person is or was a resident of Canada and is or was absent from Canada` `the person is deemed, pursuant to subsection 21(4) or (5) or under the terms of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act, not to have interrupted the person's residence in Canada during that absence` `the person was lawfully in Canada pursuant to the immigration laws of Canada immediately prior to the commencement of the absence` `the person is not or was not resident of Canada` `the person is deemed, pursuant to subsection 21(3) or under the terms of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act, to be or to have been resident in Canada` MEANS
        `the person is or was lawfully in Canada pursuant to the immigration laws of Canada in force on the applicable day`
    OR  (    `the person is or was a resident of Canada and is or was absent from Canada`
         AND `the person is deemed, pursuant to subsection 21(4) or (5) or under the terms of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act, not to have interrupted the person's residence in Canada during that absence`
         AND `the person was lawfully in Canada pursuant to the immigration laws of Canada immediately prior to the commencement of the absence`)
    OR  (    `the person is not or was not resident of Canada`
         AND `the person is deemed, pursuant to subsection 21(3) or under the terms of an agreement entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act, to be or to have been resident in Canada`)

-- 22(2): the information prescribed for section 4.1 of the Act as it relates to paragraph 4(1)(a): both a current address in
-- Canada and the reg 21(8)(a) information (a person in receipt of or approved for a plan pension) or the reg 21(8)(b) information (not).
-- src:237 | (2) For the purposes of section 4.1 of the Act as it relates to the requirement of paragraph 4(1)(a) of the Act, the prescribed information is both
-- src:238 | (a) a current address in Canada; and
-- src:239 | (b) the information that is referred to in
-- src:240 | (i) paragraph 21(8)(a), in the case of a person who is in receipt of or has been approved for a retirement, disability or survivor’s pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a retirement, disability or surviving spouse’s pension under An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan, CQLR, c. R-9, or
-- src:241 | (ii) paragraph 21(8)(b), in the case of a person who is not in receipt of and has not been approved for a retirement, disability or survivor’s pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a retirement, disability or surviving spouse’s pension under An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan, CQLR, c. R-9.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 22(2) (src:237-241)
GIVEN `the person has given a current address in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information referred to in paragraph 21(8)(a) or (b), as the case may be, has been made available` IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 21(8) above
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 22(2): the prescribed information for paragraph 4(1)(a) of the Act has been made available` `the person has given a current address in Canada` `the information referred to in paragraph 21(8)(a) or (b), as the case may be, has been made available` MEANS
        `the person has given a current address in Canada`
    AND `the information referred to in paragraph 21(8)(a) or (b), as the case may be, has been made available`
